 35CA c  J|p=0+ for {+36}Ca ground state.                                       
 35CA c  2012Sh21: A {+36}Ca secondary beam was produced via the projectile     
 35CA2c  fragmentation of a 140-MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam impinging on a 
 35CA3c  {+9}Be target at NSCL, MSU. The {+36}Ca nuclei were selected by the    
 35CA4c  A1900 separator to a purity of 8%. The ground states of {+35}K and     
 35CA5c  {+35}Ca were populated by the one-proton/neutron knockout reactions,   
 35CA6c  respectively, from the {+36}Ca beam at a midtarget energy of |?70      
 35CA7c  MeV/nucleon on a 188-mg/cm{+2} {+9}Be secondary target. Knockout       
 35CA8c  residues were identified from their energy loss measured by an         
 35CA9c  ionization chamber at the focal plane of the S800 spectrometer and from
 35CAAc  their ToF measured between two scintillators at the object position and
 35CABc  at the focal plane of the S800 spectrometer. The CsI(Na) |g-ray        
 35CACc  spectrometer CAESAR was placed around the Be target position of the    
 35CADc  S800 to search for |g decay of any excited states of the residuals     
 35CAEc  formed in knockout reactions. Measured knockout cross sections for     
 35CAFc  producing {+35}K and {+35}Ca from {+36}Ca and the longitudinal momentum
 35CAGc  distribution of residuals. Deduced J, |p, orbital angular momenta of   
 35CAHc  the nucleons removed from {+36}Ca, and spectroscopic factors.          
 35CAIc  Calculated single-particle cross sections (|s{-sp}) for neutron removal
 35CAJc  and longitudinal momentum distributions using eikonal models.          
